  description: 'Tennessine is a superheavy artificial chemical element with an atomic
    number of 117 and a symbol of Ts. Also known as eka-astatine or element 117,
    it is the second-heaviest known element and penultimate element of the 7th period
    of the periodic table. As of 2016, fifteen tennessine atoms have been observed:
    six when it was first synthesized in 2010, seven in 2012, and two in 2014.'
